at these precise moments in time. 
*   Because the values of $x_1$ itself at these switching points are not 
constant (the amplitude is decaying over time), the switch is clearly triggered 
by the state reaching a specific value of the derivative ($\dot{x}_1 = 0$) 
rather than a specific value of $x_1$ itself.

