second derivatives of the position $x$ (from `state[0, :]`) using finite        
differences to obtain velocity $\dot{x}$ and acceleration $\ddot{x}$. I'll      
analyze the relationship $\ddot{x} = f(\dot{x}, x, x^3, u)$ by attempting a     
global linear regression and then checking for residuals or discontinuities that
might indicate multiple modes (e.g., changes in the damping or stiffness        
